// Mixin marker classes — Wave-2 v1.0 minimum.
//
// Comparable / Orderable / RangeIterable are exposed as realm globals so
// user code can `addProto(Comparable)` (etc.) on its own classes for
// vocabulary alignment with the legacy stdlib.  The methods that the
// legacy share/urbi/{comparable,orderable,range-iterable}.u define
// (`!=` from `==`, `>` `<=` `>=` from `<`, map/filter/find from each)
// require closure upvalue capture and multi-slot class bodies, neither
// of which is in v1.0 scope.  Until those land, the mixins ship as
// empty-body markers — embedders attach methods externally if needed.
//
// Orderable extends Comparable in legacy.  We declare it without an
// explicit `: public Comparable` proto to keep the v1.0 chain shallow
// (deep multi-level chains with fragile method-resolution semantics
// are deferred to v1.x).  User code that wants the inheritance still
// gets it via `Bar.addProto(Comparable); Bar.addProto(Orderable)`.

class Comparable    {} |
class Orderable     {} |
class RangeIterable {} |
